# Code Quality Requirements

## Phase 1: Database & Entities
All entities must follow these rules:

### Entity Structure
- Must be in [src/database/entities/](mdc:src/database/entities)
- Must have proper TypeORM decorators
- Must include proper indexes for frequently queried fields
- Must implement soft delete where appropriate
- Must have proper cascade rules defined

### Required Fields
- `id`: UUID primary key
- `createdAt`: Creation timestamp
- `updatedAt`: Update timestamp
- `deletedAt`: For soft delete (if applicable)
- `metadata`: JSON field for extensibility

### Relationships
- Must define proper foreign key constraints
- Must specify onDelete behavior
- Must include appropriate cascade options
- Must be properly indexed

### Examples
Good entity structure:
```typescript
@Entity()
@Index(['name'])
export class Category {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')
  id: string;

  @Column()
  @Index()
  name: string;

  @CreateDateColumn()
  createdAt: Date;
}
```

